msgid "Sites that republish the feed automatically then link back to the original article, so search engines see where it first appeared."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1611
msgid "Lists of articles: an excerpt and a link instead of the full text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1611
msgid "Many themes print the whole text of every article on the home page, in categories, archives and search, so one request gives a scraper ten articles. With this on, visitors see an excerpt and a “Read the full article” link there, and each article has to be opened (and counted toward the page limit) on its own. The article pages do not change; the staff in “Who is exempt” see the full text. Changes how your lists look, so check them after turning it on. Always on in Emergency Mode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1616
msgid "XML-RPC"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1618
msgid "Turn off pingbacks"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1618
msgid "pingback.ping stays open even when XML-RPC is \"disabled\", and is used to make your site send requests to other sites or to check which pages exist. This removes the two pingback methods and the X-Pingback header; other XML-RPC methods (e.g. Jetpack) keep working. You no longer receive pingbacks from other blogs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1622
msgid "Versions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1624
msgid "Hide the versions of WordPress, PHP and the plugins"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1624
msgid "Scanners read these versions and look them up in lists of known vulnerabilities. This removes the “generator” tag from the page head and the feeds, the X-Powered-By header with the PHP version, and replaces “?ver=7.1.3” on CSS and JS files with a code that changes when the version changes, so caches still work. The readme and changelog files of WordPress and the plugins are static files: the Nginx and Apache rules in the “Server rules” tab refuse them. It does not fix any vulnerability: keep WordPress and the plugins updated."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1628
msgid "Uploads"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1630
#: includes/class-pncp-health.php:472
msgid "No PHP in the uploads folder"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1630
msgid "Files uploaded to the site (images, documents) never need to run as code. A backdoor uploaded through a vulnerable plugin usually lands in the uploads folder, so this refuses every PHP file there. On Apache it is written into the .htaccess of the uploads folder at once; on Nginx add the rule from the “Server rules” tab. If a plugin of yours really runs PHP from the uploads folder (rare), leave it off."
msgstr ""

